# Golden RBAC baseline of ClusterRole/garage-operator-manager-role — the grant a
# consumer binds when it narrows this artifact to namespace scope (README.md
# § Security posture -> Namespace-scoped operation). Gated by
# `task validate:rbac-narrowing`, declared by `compatibility.yaml rbac_policy`.
#
# One normalized `<apiGroup>|<resource>|<verb>` triple per line, `LC_ALL=C sort -u`
# order; the core API group is the empty string, hence a leading `|`. Comment and
# blank lines are ignored by the gate.
#
# WHY a golden and not just a schema: a consumer's per-namespace RoleBinding
# references this ClusterRole BY NAME, so any upstream rule the chart adds on a bump
# silently widens every narrowed consumer's grant. A diff against this file is the
# only place that change becomes visible before publish. Authored from the chart
# source (`vendor/garage-operator-0.7.3.tgz` templates/clusterrole.yaml), not from
# the gate's own output.
#
# Updating it is deliberate: re-derive from the chart, review the delta as a grant
# change, and re-check the README's cost statement and `inert_when_namespaced`.
